  "tags": ["alerting", "incident", "sre"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "Effective alerting notifies the right people of actionable issues. Bad alerting causes alert fatigue."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Alert",
            "definition": "A notification that requires action."
          },
          {
            "term": "Alert Fatigue",
            "definition": "Ignoring alerts due to too many false positives."
          },
          {
            "term": "SLO",
            "definition": "Service Level Objective: a target for service reliability."
          },
          {
            "term": "Error Budget",
            "definition": "The acceptable amount of unreliability."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Alert Design Principles"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Actionable: every alert requires action",
          "Clear: indicates what is wrong and how to fix",
          "Timely: fires when action is needed",
          "Not noisy: avoid alert fatigue"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "What to Alert On"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "data": {
        "headers": ["Signal", "Example", "Severity"],
        "rows": [
          ["Error rate", "Error rate > 1%", "High"],
          ["Latency", "p99 > 500ms", "Medium"],
          ["Saturation", "CPU > 90%", "Medium"],
          ["Business", "Orders dropping", "High"]
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "SLOs and Error Budgets"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "SLOs define reliability targets. Error budgets define acceptable unreliability. Alert when error budget is being consumed too fast."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Alert Routing"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Page for critical, actionable alerts",
          "Ticket for non-critical issues",
          "Log for informational events",
          "Suppress during maintenance"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
